To create a Discord bot that communicates with the server using WebSockets, you'll need to follow these steps:

1. Set up your development environment:
   - Install Node.js and npm (Node Package Manager) from https://nodejs.org/
   - Install Discord.js by running `npm install discord.js` in your terminal or command prompt

2. Create a new Discord application:
   - Go to the Discord Developer Portal (https://discord.com/developers/applications) and click on "New Application"
   - Fill out the required information and click "Create"
   - In the "Bot" tab, click on "Add Bot" and follow the prompts to create a bot user
   - Note down the bot token, as you'll need it later

3. Create a Discord bot:
   - In your terminal or command prompt, run `npx discordjs-create bot` to create a new Discord bot project
   - Navigate to the newly created directory and open the `main.js` file

4. Configure the bot:
   - Replace the placeholders in the `main.js` file with your Discord application's ID and bot token
   - Set up the WebSocket connection by adding the following code:

```javascript
const { Client, Events, GatewayIntentBits } = require('discord.js');
const client = new Client({ intents: [GatewayIntentBits.Guilds, GatewayIntentBits.GuildMessages] });

client.once(Events.ClientReady, () => {
  console.log('Connected to Discord!');
});

client.on(Events.MessageCreate, (message) => {
  if (message.author.bot) return;
  if (message.content === 'ping') {
    message.reply('Pong!');
  }
});

client.connect();
```

5. Run the bot:
   - Run `npm start` in your terminal or command prompt to start the bot
   - The bot will connect to the Discord server and listen for messages

