To identify the tense of a given sentence, we need to analyze the verbs in the sentence. Here's a simple MATLAB code that can do that:

```matlab
function tense = identify_tense(sentence)
    % Split the sentence into words
    words = strsplit(sentence, ' ');

    % Initialize the tense variable
    tense = '';

    % Loop through the words and check if they are verbs
    for i = 1:length(words)
        % Check if the word is a verb (e.g., ends with -ing or -s)
        if strcmp(words{i}, words{i}) || strcmp(words{i}, words{i} + 'ing') || strcmp(words{i}, words{i} + 's')
            % Determine the tense of the verb
            if strcmp(words{i}, words{i} + 'ing')
                tense = 'Present Continuous';
            elseif strcmp(words{i}, words{i} + 's')
                tense = 'Present Simple';
            end

            % Break out of the loop once a verb is found
            break;
        end
    end
end

