To implement a peer-to-peer (P2P) protocol with Node.js and MongoDB for building a blockchain system, follow these steps:

1. Set up the development environment:
   - Install Node.js and npm (Node Package Manager) from https://nodejs.org/
   - Install MongoDB Community Server from https://www.mongodb.com/try/download/community

2. Create a new project directory:
   ```
   mkdir blockchain-p2p
   cd blockchain-p2p
   ```

3. Initialize a new npm project:
   ```
   npm init -y
   ```

4. Install required dependencies:
   ```
   npm install express body-parser mongoose
   ```

5. Create a `server.js` file to set up the P2P server:
   ```javascript
   // server.js
   const express = require('express');
   const bodyParser = require('body-parser');
   const mongoose = require('mongoose');

   const app = express();
   app.use(bodyParser.json());

   // Connect to MongoDB
   mongoose.connect('mongodb://localhost/blockchain', { useNewUrlParser: true, useUnifiedTopology: true })
     .then(() => console.log('Connected to MongoDB'))
     .catch(err => console.error('Error connecting to MongoDB:', err));

   // Define the Block schema
   const BlockSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
     data: Buffer,
     hash: String,
     previousHash: String,
     timestamp: Date,
