In each service, create a REST controller to handle CRUD operations on the domain entities. Use Spring MVC or Spring Web to create the controllers.

Example:
```java
// UserController.java
@RestController
public class UserController {
    @Autowired
    private UserService userService;

    @GetMapping("/users")
    public List<User> getUsers() {
        return userService.getUsers();
    }

    @PostMapping("/users")
    public User createUser(@RequestBody User user) {
        return userService.createUser(user);
    }

    // Other CRUD operations
}
```

3. Implement the service layer:
Create a separate folder for your service layers, and implement the business logic for each service. Use Spring DI to inject dependencies into the services.

Example:
```java
// UserService.java
@Service
public class UserService {
    @Autowired
    private UserRepository userRepository;

    public List<User> getUsers() {
        return userRepository.findAll();
    }

    public User createUser(User user) {
        return userRepository.save(user);
    }

    // Other business logic
}
```

