Yes, you can upload images to MongoDB using the `GridFS` (Grid File System) feature. GridFS is a way of storing and retrieving large files, such as images, within MongoDB. It allows you to store files as chunks, which are then stored in the database as separate documents. This approach makes it easier to manage and retrieve large files, especially when working with databases that have limited storage capacity or slow network connections.

