Here's a React utility to remove widows:

```javascript
import React, { useEffect } from 'react';

const RemoveWidows = ({ children }) => {
  useEffect(() => {
    const words = children.split(' ');
    const lastWordIndex = words.length - 1;

    if (lastWordIndex >= 0 && words[lastWordIndex].length > 1) {
      const lastWord = words[lastWordIndex];
      const newLastWord = lastWord.substring(0, lastWord.length - 1);

      words[lastWordIndex] = newLastWord;
      children = words.join(' ');
    }
  }, [children]);

  return <div>{children}</div>;
};

export default RemoveWidows;
```

This component takes a `children` prop, which is the text content of the component. It splits the text into an array of words, finds the last word, and removes the last letter if it's a vowel. Finally, it joins the words back together and returns the modified text.

